# Fixture — the 2026-10-18 01:38 UTC PipelineWatchdog race (card t_b72dce57).
# Seeded verbatim from the real ~/.hscc/daemon.log.1.gz (lines covering
# 01:36:25–01:39:10 UTC); the ONLY edit is the sanctioned address redaction
# (live LAN hosts -> 10.0.0.x placeholders — scripts/address_guard.py owns the
# rule). Timestamps, levels and message text are kept exactly as logged,
# including the cosmetic "deferred — deferred —" double-prefix in the proxy
# WARN (health.py builds that message from a prefix that already says
# "deferred"; fixing cosmetics is not this card's scope).
#
# What happened, in order:
#   * 01:36:25 / 01:37:29  the engine-wedge probe reports 'orch' WEDGED twice.
#   * 01:38:29             engine-wedge recovery crosses the streak=3 threshold,
#                          takes the autodown lock + the heal lease
#                          ("engine-wedge-recovery (orch)"), stops 'orch'
#                          (stop_ok=True) and relaunches it via
#                          `hscc cluster up` — the CORRECT job (03fae933, with
#                          the served_model_name aliases).
#   * 01:38:34             the proxy stream finds the lease held and DEFERS.
#                          The lock exists and works here.
#   * 01:38:44             10s later the PipelineWatchdog tick sees DGX/Gateway
#                          down and IGNORES the lease: it issues its own vLLM
#                          restart.
#   * 01:38:45             its stop is the target-less `sparkrun stop --hosts
#                          <node>`, which sparkrun rejects ("Must specify
#                          TARGET or --all") — nothing was stopped — and the
#                          code continued anyway.
#   * 01:39:09             the launch "succeeded": a SECOND job from the bare
#                          recipe (no served_model_name; recipe_fingerprint
#                          9c2c08c6ba56 vs the correct 256790855d81) landed on
#                          10.0.0.244 while :8000 was still held by the correct
#                          job, so vllm inside it never started (container ran
#                          `sleep infinity` only) — a HOLLOW launch, and the
#                          counter/notification recorded it as success. Both
#                          jobs sat in ~/.hscc/state/dgx.json ~7h until the
#                          operator stopped the hollow one manually.
# The replay tests in test_lifecycle_watchdog_race_20261018.py assert the NEW
# behaviour (deferral only, no stop, no launch, no hollow success) against this
# exact window, and pin the OLD behaviour (stop-then-launch despite the lease)
# against the mutation probes.
